observation-watcher 2026/06/08 00:56:28 new observation timestamp=2026-06-08T00:56:26Z source=entity-graph status=needs_attention subject="Entity graph run: 8 filings, 36 directors, 0 proposals, 89 signals" hash=b63596cdd43d
Done. Here's a summary of what was done:

**Root cause:** `extractProposals()` and `extractAuditor()` in `parser.go` used an inline regex matching only `Proposal N` format. Actual EDGAR Item 5.07 filings use two different formats not covered by that regex:
- **ABBV-style parenthesised:** `(2) The stockholders ratified the appointment of...`
- **BA-style bare-number:** `2. Advisory Vote on Named Executive Officer Compensation: FOR AGAINST ABSTAIN...`

**Fix:** Promoted the inline `proposalSplitter` to a package-level `reProposalSplitter` covering all three formats:
```
(?i)(?:Proposal\s+(?:[2-9]|1\d)\b|\((?:[2-9]|1\d)\)\s|\b(?:[2-9]|1\d)\.\s+[A-Z])
```

Both `extractProposals()` and `extractAuditor()` now use this shared regex. Two new tests added (`TestParseItem507_ParenthesisedProposals`, `TestParseItem507_BareNumberProposals`). Full test suite passes. Committed as `2c8d809` and pushed.
observation-watcher 2026/06/08 01:05:19 new observation timestamp=2026-06-08T00:59:47Z source=entity-graph status=needs_attention subject="Entity graph run: 7 filings, 36 directors, 0 proposals, 3 signals" hash=ead6aa02b222
Run complete. Here's a summary of what was done:

**Context:** The observation (2026-06-08T00:59:47Z) reported 0 proposals parsed despite 36 directors found. The core fix (adding parenthesised `(2)` and bare-number `2.` proposal formats to the splitter regex) had already been committed in the prior RSI run (2c8d809).

**This run's changes** (commit `a013650`):

1. **`reRatificationProposal`** — added `ratified` (past tense) to the alternation. ABBV-2026 says "The stockholders **ratified** the appointment of Ernst & Young LLP…" — neither "ratification" nor "ratifying" matched. Auditor extraction still worked via the "independent registered public accounting" fallback, but this makes the detection explicit and robust for filings that omit that phrase.

2. **`reDidNotPass`** — added `did\s+not\s+approve`. ABBV-2026 proposal (4) says "The stockholders did not approve the management proposal regarding amendment…to eliminate supermajority voting" with 98.7% for-vote (implicit supermajority). The parser was marking it `Passed=true`; it now correctly sets `Passed=false`.

3. **New real-data fixture** — `fixtures/entitygraph/abbv_8k_5_07_2026.txt` with test `TestParseItem507_ABBV2026` covering all four proposals including the `did not approve` case. All 57+ tests pass.
observation-watcher 2026/06/08 03:12:31 new observation timestamp=2026-06-08T03:12:27Z source=entity-graph status=needs_attention subject="Entity graph run: 5 filings, 52 directors, 0 proposals, 12 signals" hash=215015001305
Done. Here's what was found and fixed:

**Root cause**: AMZN annual meeting 8-Ks from 2010–2015 use prose-style proposal descriptions with no numbered headers. Each proposal starts with a sentence like `"The appointment of Ernst & Young LLP as our independent auditor was ratified by the vote set forth below:"` — invisible to `reProposalSplitter`, which only recognises `Proposal N`, `(N)`, `N.`, `N Title`, `Item N`, and `b) B...` formats.

**Fix** (`internal/entitygraph/parser.go`):
- Added `reProseSplitter` regex covering 5 AMZN prose-format proposal openers: `The appointment of`, `A/An shareholder/stockholder proposal`, `An advisory vote`, `The compensation of our named`, `The material terms of the`
- `extractProposals()` now calls `extractProseProposals()` as a fallback **only** when the primary numbered-format splitter returns 0 results — this ensures SCHW/ABBV/BA/BLK/LLY filings containing these phrases inside numbered proposal blocks are never re-split
- `extractAuditor()` refactored to try both splitters, so auditor names are correctly captured from AMZN filings too

**Tests**: 3 new tests added; full `go test ./...` passes. Commit `f76090a` pushed.

**Side note**: The updated observation (03:15Z) shows a spurious `nomination_rejection` for entity "Equity Disclosure" at SCHW — that's a false-positive director-name extraction worth a follow-up review of `looksLikePersonName()`.
