## What was investigated and fixed

**Root cause of "0 proposals" observation:** The entity-graph daemon was running with pre-fix code (started before the 06:49 commit) — all batch runs today used the old binary. The parser code itself was already correct; the gap was from the running process.

**New bug found and fixed (`b00377f`):** `reDirectorRow` was scanning the entire Item 5.07 body including non-director proposal blocks. In BA-style annual meeting 8-Ks (2010–2025), shareholder proposals end with title-case phrases before vote counts — e.g. `"...Human Rights Code 36,584,516 418,543,421 75,589,953"`. The last two title-cased words ("Rights Code", "Political Activity") passed `looksLikePersonName` and were stored as director nodes with ~7% approval, generating **false-positive `nomination_rejection` signals at critical severity** — the exact entities seen in the observation's high-severity signals.

**Fix:** `ParseItem507` now truncates the body passed to `extractDirectorVotes` at the first `reProposalSplitter` boundary. `extractProposals` and `extractAuditor` continue to use the full body. BA 2010–2025 annual meetings now extract 8–13 real directors (was 13–14) with no spurious entries.

**Test added:** `TestParseItem507_BAProposalNoSpuriousDirectors` covering this exact case. All 68+ tests pass.
