## Summary

**Report: Token Efficiency RSI — Cycle 4**

### Token Spend Analysis

| Subsystem | Per-cycle overhead | Status |
|---|---|---|
| **FatBaby /tick tool loop** | System+tools: ~5,400T (cached). Conversation history: 80T+400T/turn (NOT cached until now) | Fixed this cycle |
| **EMILY cron.go RSI loop** | Generator + evaluator: ~700T system prompt each, 2 calls/iter | Fixed cycle 2 (57cfb90) |
| **observation-watcher dispatch** | runReportFooter ~450T + task content; separate subprocess per task | Batching done cycle 3 |

### Prioritized Improvements

| # | Improvement | Estimated Savings |
|---|---|---|
| ✅ 1 | Conversation history caching in `runToolLoop` | ~2,000–4,500T per 5–10 turn tick |
| 2 | Prime-task batching (N tasks → 1 invocation) | N-1 invocation overheads/burst |
| 3 | Entity-graph rules inline skip (hash-unchanged) | ~320T/entity-graph dispatch |

### Change Made

**`cmd/emily-agent/main.go`** — Added `cache_control: {type: ephemeral}` to the last tool-result block in each `runToolLoop` iteration. The Anthropic API caches the full conversation history through the previous turn; each new turn only pays fresh for its own content (~400-800T vs the full 1,500-4,500T accumulated history).

