**Summary of this run:**

**Token efficiency report findings:**

| Component | Per-cycle spend | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Emily Prime RSI loop (cron.go) | ~10K–16K tokens | 2 LLM calls (generator + evaluator); system prompts already cached |
| Observation-watcher dispatch | ~75K–200K tokens | Dominated by Claude Code session; batch window + gate already active |
| Prime-task → Claude Code | **Unlimited** before fix | rsi-loop.sh fires same preset every 30s; no dedup for CLI-written tasks |

**Prioritized improvements:**

1. **Prime-task dedup gate in `pollPrimeTasks()`** — 3M–15M tokens/day saved ← **implemented**
2. RSI generator/evaluator static-prefix caching — ~3,600T/task (requires `CachedPrefix` field in `LLMRequest`)
3. `Pipeline.Run()` turn-level caching in Emily Prime — ~4,500T/session (mirrors what FatBaby already does)

**Implementation:** Added `primeTaskDuplicateExists()` and `primeDedupWindow=4h` to `cmd/observation-watcher/main.go`. Before Claude Code is invoked for a prime task, the function scans the tasks directory for any other file within 4 hours with the same `task_type + description`. If found, the cursor advances (file marked seen) but no Claude session is spawned. Commit `4b2f34c`, IDUNA Apple #268.
