Apple #591 filed. All mandatory steps complete.

---

## Summary

Three DIS pre-deploy bugs fixed in EDIS commit `fad4f6d`:

**Bug 1 — nginx parser zero records** (`cmd/dis/main.go`): `parseNginxCombined` used `SplitN(line, " ", 9)` with status at `parts[8]`. When nginx logs `"-"` for malformed requests (no internal spaces), STATUS shifts to `parts[6]` and `parts[8]` = referer string → `ParseUint("-")` fails → all 400-class lines dropped. Fixed by finding `$request` via its surrounding double-quotes and parsing status/bytes from `line[reqClose+2:]`. This restores ingestion of exactly the scanner/bot traffic DIS is built to score.

**Bug 2 — posture window race** (`internal/dis/posture.go`): `recompute()` swapped `totalN` then `hostileN`. A goroutine racing between the two swaps contributed to `hostileN` (numerator) but NOT `totalN` (denominator) → inflated `hostile_ratio` → premature attack escalation. Fixed: swap `hostileN` first, `totalN` second — racing goroutines now land in the denominator only, keeping ratio conservative.

**Bug 3 — missing hostile_ratio** (`cmd/dis/main.go`, `edis-dis.php`): Added `hostile_ratio` field to `healthResponse` JSON and wired to `p.HostileRatio()`; added Hostile Ratio row to the WordPress admin posture panel.

13 new tests cover all three fixes including a specific `bad_request_dash` regression test.
